<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Florence Cathedral</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1296–1436</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Santa Maria del Fiore</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> Cathedral, the Cattedrale di Santa Maria del Fiore, is the cathedral of Florence, begun in 1296 to designs by Arnolfo di Cambio and consecrated in 1436. Its octagonal dome by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/filippo-brunelleschi">Filippo Brunelleschi</a>, completed in 1436, was the largest built since antiquity, and with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giotto">Giotto</a>'s bell tower and the Baptistery the cathedral forms the centre of the historic city, a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/florence-cathedral.jpg" alt="Florence Cathedral" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gary Campbell-Hall · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cattedrale_di_Santa_Maria_del_Fiore_%E2%80%93_Il_Duomo_di_Firenze.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
